# promise: #600
# Arc's Duplicate on a favorite's menu and on a split's menu (GitHub #600): the tab rows' menu had it,
# the favorite tile's and the split's did not. As in Arc 1.173.1 (checked live 19 Nov), a favorite's
# copy is a Today tab where new tabs go, not another favorite, and a favorite split's copy is a Today
# split; the copies stay in the background, so the open tab stays open.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=fav
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=left
cra://action/addSplitView
cra://navigate?url=${PAGE}?n=right
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
wait 1

cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=tab
expect-log favorite menu tab: Copy Link\|Share ▸\|──\|Change Icon…\|Tile Color ▸\|Rename…\|Edit Pinned URL…\|Replace Pinned URL with Current \(off\)\|Mute \(off\)\|──\|Open in Split View\|Duplicate\|──\|(Close Tab\|)?Remove Favorite$
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=tab-copy&run=Duplicate
expect-log favorite menu tab-copy favorites: n=fav n=left\+n=right today: n=fav open: n=right$
wait 1

cra://debug?favoriteMenu=2&label=split
expect-log favorite menu split: Remove from Favorites\|──\|Share Split View…\|──\|Separate All Tabs\|.*\|Rename…\|──\|Duplicate\|Move to ▸\|──\|Archive Item
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=2&label=split-copy&run=Duplicate
expect-log favorite menu split-copy favorites: n=fav n=left\+n=right today: n=left\+n=right n=fav open: n=right$
